摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"GitHub (gh) + Gitea (tea) + npm CLIs for DeepSeek Harness (dsh): guided auth/config, issue & package tools","id":"gh:1334561216","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"gh-tea-npm-dsh","slug":"TommyFang2077/gh-tea-npm-dsh","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","gh","gitea","github","github-cli","issues","nodejs","npm","package-manager","tea"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"GitHub (gh) + Gitea (tea) + npm CLIs for DeepSeek Harness (dsh): guided auth/config, issue & package"},{"id":"p1s2","text":" (gh) + Gitea (tea) + npm CLIs for DeepSeek Harness (dsh): guided auth/config, issue & package tools"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# gh-tea-npm-dsh"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English · 简体中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A DeepSeek Harness (dsh) plugin that brings **GitHub (`gh`)**, **Gitea (`tea`)**, and **npm** into t"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"he agent. It detects and installs the CLIs, guides the user through authentication with explicit cho"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"ices, and operates issues and publishes packages."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"**gh / tea**"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- detect installation, version, auth status, and token environment variables (values masked)\n- one-c"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"ommand install — Homebrew when available, otherwise a no-sudo binary into `~/.local/bin`\n- guided au"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"th: import from env, browser OAuth device flow, or manual token\n- issues: `list` · `view` · `create`"},{"id":"p7s4","text":" · `comment` · `close` · `reopen`"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"**npm**"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"- detect node/npm, login state (`npm whoami`), and registry\n- guided login: browser OAuth device flo"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"w (`npm login --auth-type=web`) or automation token\n- publish packages (`npm publish --access public"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"`)\n- **90-day token expiry notice and rotation** guidance"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"**Skill**"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"- registers a companion `gh-tea-npm` skill that documents the workflows and points at each CLI's own"},{"id":"p11s2","text":" `--help` as the authoritative command surface"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"- Node.js ≥ 18 and npm (for the npm tools)\n- `gh` and `tea` are optional — the plugin installs them "},{"id":"p13s2","text":"≥ 18 and npm (for the npm tools)\n- `gh` and `tea` are optional — the plugin installs them if missing"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"This is a host-only bundle: `cordis.patch.yml` (referenced by the package's `dsh.bundle` manifest) i"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"nserts the plugin row, and `dsh/index.js` registers the tools and the skill."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"## Guided configuration"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"The plugin never poses open-ended questions. It returns a menu, the agent presents it as options, an"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"d the user advances one step at a time."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"**gh / tea** — `gitclis_configure`:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"1. `gitclis_configure method=auto` → current state + next-step menu\n2. install a missing CLI with `g"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"itclis_install`, or pick a token source:\n- env import → `method=env`\n- browser OAuth (GitHub) → `met"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"hod=web` (returns a device code) → `method=poll` to verify\n- manual → `gitclis_set_token`\n3. verify "},{"id":"p20s4","text":"with `gitclis_status`"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"**npm** — `npm_configure`:"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"1. `npm_configure method=auto` → current state + next-step menu\n2. browser OAuth → `method=web` (ret"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"urns a login URL) → `method=poll` to verify, or automation token → `method=token`\n3. publish with `n"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"pm_publish` (or `npm_publish dry_run=true`)"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## npm token policy (90 days)"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"npm now caps access tokens — including automation tokens — at a **90-day** lifetime. An expired toke"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"n breaks `npm publish`, so rotate before it lapses:"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"- generate a new Automation token at `https://www.npmjs.com/settings/<user>/tokens/new`, then `npm_c"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"onfigure method=token`; or\n- re-run `npm_configure method=web`."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"`npm_status` surfaces this policy and `npm_configure` walks through rotation."},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Tools"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"| Tool | Description |"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"| `gitclis_status` | detect gh/tea install, version, auth, env tokens (masked) |\n| `gitclis_configur"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"e` | guided gh/tea config — `auto`/`env`/`web`/`manual`/`poll` |\n| `gitclis_install` | install gh an"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"d/or tea |\n| `gitclis_set_token` | store a gh/tea token (never echoed) |\n| `gitclis_token_env` | rea"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"d/import token environment variables |\n| `gitclis_issue_list` | list issues |\n| `gitclis_issue_view`"},{"id":"p29s5","text":" | view one issue, optionally with comments |\n| `gitclis_issue_create` | create an issue |\n| `gitcli"},{"id":"p29s6","text":"s_issue_comment` | comment on an issue |\n| `gitclis_issue_close` | close an issue |\n| `gitclis_issue"},{"id":"p29s7","text":"_reopen` | reopen an issue |\n| `npm_status` | detect node/npm, login state, registry |\n| `npm_config"},{"id":"p29s8","text":"ure` | guided npm auth — `auto`/`web`/`token`/`poll` |\n| `npm_publish` | publish to npm |"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Issue tools take a `provider` argument: `github` → `gh`, `gitea` → `tea`."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"## Skill"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"The companion skill is registered at runtime and shipped on disk at `skills/gh-tea-npm/SKILL.md`. It"},{"id":"p32s2","text":" documents issue-workflow recipes, the auth flows, and the npm token policy, and defers to `gh <cmd>"},{"id":"p32s3","text":" --help`, `tea <cmd> --help`, and `npm <cmd> --help` for exact flags."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## Repository layout"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
